data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":2105,"item_id":"msg_05281c5186fe0d91016b08fc245df087d1996260c94a061ccc","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"lin\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Develop a general targeted food-constituent test operation with assessment and assay modes. The related-capability search and supplied registry identify observation, physical probing, drying and relative-mass comparison, but none provides a selective dietary-constituent measurement. probe cannot establish toxin concentration; compare-material-samples and air-dry-food-trial are limited to berries or roots and explicitly exclude safety evidence; beam-mass-comparator supplies relative mass, not an absolute analytical calibration. Their limitations must not be bypassed by renaming their outputs. There is currently no supported executable dietary assay for item-11-lin-103. A prerequisite assessment and a conditional, physically grounded assay contract are reasonable development, not grounds for permanent rejection. No testing, learning or world-time advancement starts with this review.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"General operation: targeted-food-constituent-test(targetItemId, constituent, methodRef, mode, sampleMass, equipmentIds, reagentIds, referenceIds), with assess, run, inspect, resume and cancel modes. Applicable to any owned food sample for which the selected analytical method is validated, not exclusively hazelnuts or this item. Implement in the current-conversation development handoff. The smallest immediately executable mode is a bounded prerequisite assessment that returns missing requirements and an explicit inability to measure; the physical assay remains disabled until its concrete method dependencies are implemented and present. Do not implement an arbitrary toxin value, imaginary sensor or substitute mass loss for dietary evidence.\\\\nConcrete initial assay family: a matrix-validated competitive immunoassay for total aflatoxins, explicitly defined as the measured sum of B1, B2, G1 and G2 under the selected method's documented cross-reactivity and recovery limitations. This is one possible dietary property, not a claim that this nut contains aflatoxins. Required methodRef is an exact manufacturer, product, revision and lot-specific instruction/calibration reference explicitly validating hazelnut or the applicable nut matrix. No such reference, kit or validation has been supplied. The current assessment must therefore report: no aflatoxin measurement available; kit/method validation, absolute sample-mass measurement, clean preparation equipment, extraction liquid, volumetric equipment, assay consumables, controls, reader and safe waste handling are unestablished. It must not disclose any hidden constituent, item mass, contamination or inventory fact.\\\\nReferences and provenance: use targetItemId=item-11-lin-103 only as this applicant's proposed argument; retain its origin start-1-nuts and existing sample history. item-11-lin-103:observed-state, evidence event-15-lin-150, and start-1-nuts:observed-state, evidence event-9-lin-84, are observations, not dietary measurements. The berry knowledge record is not evidence about hazelnuts. Record implementation reuse of existing ownership, quantity, decay, action charging and event infrastructure where available; cite probe/open.probe, foundation-open@1 if its observation or interaction handler is actually reused. Do not claim the selective assay is already implemented by probe or reinvent existing mass-comparison or drying code.\\\\nAssessment costs one active round and 0.2 energy, consumes no sample or reagent, and examines only supplied or otherwise authorized accessible evidence. It cannot conjure equipment or inspect hidden chemical state. Report the exact method-dependent bill of materials and timing if a method is available; otherwise list these as unresolved, with no trial enabled. This limitation report is a real assessment output but is not itself a chemical result.\\\\nBefore run is accepted, lock a complete executable recipe from methodRef: required sample mass in grams; amount and identity of each solvent, diluent and reagent; extraction ratio and duration; grinding requirements; aliquot and dilution volumes; incubation/read windows; controls; calibration; detection and quantitation limits; reportable range; matrix recovery and cross-reactivity limits; units and uncertainty; disposal conditions. Availability is unknown, not assumed. A calibrated absolute balance and appropriate volumetric tools are required; the relative beam comparator alone cannot satisfy these requirements. If the single nut cannot supply the recipe's minimum sample, report insufficient sample rather than scaling an unvalidated method. Consumables, standards, tools and protective provisions must be actual accessible resources with explicit IDs, ownership/use authority, quantities and condition. Hazardous solvents require suitable containment, ventilation, ignition separation and waste storage before opening. Never taste or feed the sample to anyone.\\\\nThe physical sequence is to weigh the permitted sample, homogenize the required edible portion without adding material, extract using the specified measured liquid, separate and dilute the specified aliquot, run the blank and method-required negative/positive or recovery controls, expose the assay to the aliquot, and read it at the specified time with its compatible calibrated reader. Interpretation must be calculated in code from the recorded physical assay response and valid calibration, including dilution and sample-mass factors. If the simulation has no implemented selective response mechanism or validated method record, run is unavailable and assessment reports that limitation; it may not read latent food toxicity directly. Implementing that mechanism and its dependency validation belongs in this development handoff, not an invented sequence of unrelated activities or an era unlock.\\\\nCosts and progress: assess and inspect each cost one round and 0.2 energy. Each accepted hands-on assay step costs one active round and 0.5 energy; longer timed operations and equipment energy follow the locked recipe and must be included in a pre-run quote. Incubation/extraction time advances only through actual simulation rounds, with a declared conversion to method time; development or review waiting advances nothing. Reject an unquotable or unschedulable recipe before charging or reserving inputs. Show exact expected active rounds, elapsed rounds, energy, consumables and destructive sample mass before the applicant separately starts. Record completed steps, actual quantities, timestamps, instrument/calibration IDs and next deadlines; charge only performed work. No automatic testing, acquisition or communication. Other participants, if any, must communicate and perform their own actions independently.\\\\nConservation: reserve only the authorized sample portion and consumables, retain original provenance and ordinary decay, and subtract actual weighed material without inventing a unit-to-gram conversion. If calibrated splitting is not supported, require the whole item and report the destruction involved. Homogenate, shell if removed, retained food, spent extract, used assay and solvent waste remain explicit material outputs; aliquots cannot be duplicated and used analytical material cannot be returned as clean food. Reagent volumes and evaporation or transfers require corresponding material accounting. Assay results neither restore nutrition nor remove toxins. The untested remainder, if any, retains its prior state; no measured concentration is assigned to it automatically.\\\\nInterruption, cancellation and death stop hands-on work and release unused reservations once; spent sample, energy, reagents and elapsed time are never refunded. Resume only from logged steps whose contamination, storage and timing conditions remain valid. A missed read window or failed control produces invalid/inconclusive output and a new attempt requires new consumed inputs. Timed chemical processes and ordinary spoilage continue while the world actually advances, even if the actor stops; they do not continue during review waiting. Death cancels the active assignment without resurrecting inputs or automatically disposing of hazards. Leave labeled materials, waste and equipment in their real locations. No autonomous repeat assays or ongoing benefit. Maintain tools by required cleaning and calibration checks; damaged, contaminated or expired equipment/reagents fail prerequisite checks.\\\\nResult scope: a valid result reports only the named analyte sum in the analyzed homogenate, with method, units, uncertainty/range, controls and sample provenance. Below detection means not detected at that method's limit, not absent. Out-of-range and invalid controls must be explicit. A single nut is not a representative batch sample. Results do not establish absence of other toxins, allergens, microbes, rancidity or nutritional inadequacy, general edibility, a necessary preparation, successful detoxification or health improvement. No roasting/treatment recommendation follows without separate validated evidence. The current assessment must conclude that none of those dietary properties has yet been measured.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":5,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Lin must individually study for 5 active rounds at 0.5 energy per completed round; record progress, pause/resume it, and do not refund completed study. Study does not supply tools, evidence, consent or mastery in advance. Requests, registration, assessment checklists, missing-resource reports and learning grant no pleasure or satisfaction. A completed assay may qualify only for a personally applicable, genuinely verified information gain; a failed assay qualifies only if controls or observations actually establish a new bounded fact, not merely because it failed. If using the existing experience system, deduplicate by sample provenance, analyte, method and materially changed evidence; cap any eligible event at 0.2 short pleasure, at most once per 10 actual rounds, decaying to zero within 10 rounds, and at most 0.04 maintained satisfaction gain per eligible round with the existing 0.002 decay and existing account cap. Repeated equivalent readings cannot farm novelty rewards. These are event eligibility bounds, not permission to alter protected reward accounts, budgets, goals or permissions; if the existing protected interface cannot express them, issue no reward. No nutrition, health or physical-comfort benefit is granted.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Emit observable assessment, step-start, material-transfer, timed-process, control-read, invalidation, cancellation and completed-result events only when those actions actually occur. Reusable visual metadata should include capability/mode, actor and target IDs, method reference, stage, progress, elapsed/deadline rounds, equipment/material IDs, location and status (requirements-missing, ready, active, paused, invalid, cancelled or result-available). Show real tools, sample preparation, containers and waste only when present. Any assay coloration or reader indication requires a modeled physical response and appropriate visibility; an assessment cannot display a completed test. Display result provenance, limits and invalid/inconclusive states alongside readings. No green safe-to-eat badge, treatment-success animation, imagined laboratory, toxin visualization, mastery effect or reward celebration for incomplete or failed work.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

